# Example reverse-proxy config for Caddy (https://caddyserver.com) — the
# simplest way to get free, automatic HTTPS in front of this app. Caddy
# handles certificate provisioning and renewal (via Let's Encrypt)
# entirely on its own; you don't touch certificates at all.
#
# 1. Point your domain's DNS A record at your server's IP first.
# 2. Save this as Caddyfile (no extension) on your server.
# 3. Replace the domain below with your real one.
# 4. Run: caddy run
#
# That's the whole HTTPS setup — Caddy gets a certificate automatically
# the first time it starts, and renews it automatically forever after.

yourdomain.com {
	reverse_proxy localhost:4000
}

# If you're also configuring the Paystack webhook, its public URL will be:
#   https://yourdomain.com/api/webhooks/paystack
# Paste that into your Paystack dashboard under Settings -> API Keys & Webhooks.
